<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55952" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηχ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sound over</i> or <i>through</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁρμονία κ. τῆς θαλάττης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					1.19
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				2.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>sound amiss</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνηχέω</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Vitr.
				5.8.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>teach by word of mouth</i>: hence generally, <i>instruct</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τινὰ πολλὰ τῶν
			ἀγνοουμένων</span> Agrippa <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>Vit.</u>
				65
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Asin.</u>
				48
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PStrassb.</u>
				41.37
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be informed</i> or <i>instructed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					21.21
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὅτι</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.575
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ κατηχήμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					5.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in <i>NT,
				instruct in the elements of religion</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Cor.</u>
				14.19
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ ὧν κατηχήθης λόγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
					1.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κατηχούμενος τὸν λόγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Gal.</u>
					6.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηχημένος τὴν ὁδὸν τοῦ Κυρίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					18.25
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Chr.</u>
				26
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
